  "body": "<div align=\"center\">\n  <img src=\"https://cdn.tw93.fun/pic/cole.png\" alt=\"Mole Logo\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" style=\"border-radius:50%\" />\n  <h1 style=\"margin: 12px 0 6px;\">Mole</h1>\n  <p><em>Deep clean and optimize your Mac.</em></p>\n</div>\n\n### Changelog\n\n1. **Slim universal apps on Apple Silicon**: `mo slim` removes the Intel code from apps you own, slims each one on a copy that must pass code signing and Gatekeeper checks before it replaces the original, moves the original to the Trash, and needs no developer tools; preview with `mo slim --dry-run`.\n2. **Let your AI agent drive Mole**: The official Mole skill teaches Claude Code, Codex, Cursor and other agents to preview every cleanup with `--dry-run` and leave uninstalls and admin steps to you; install it with `npx skills add tw93/Mole -a claude-code codex cursor -g -y`.\n3. **Uninstall with personal data selected**: `mo uninstall --with-data <name>` starts with the app's settings and data selected, still lists them in the preview, and `D` lets you keep any path.\n4. **Clean more app leftovers**: Clean reaches Feishu and its sandboxed caches, WeChat web profiles, idle Helium signing clones and Futu NiuNiu update downloads while Futu is closed.\n5. **Correct external drive cleanup**: `mo clean --external` reports the space it actually freed, keeps the drive's Trash and protected Finder metadata, and sizes a temporary folder with an unreadable child instead of skipping it.\n6. **Safer uninstall prompts**: Homebrew cask password prompts stay in the foreground, every real uninstall needs an interactive confirmation, a dry run without a terminal ends with its plan, and app names with control characters print safely.\n7. **No Command Line Tools prompt on update**: On a Mac without developer tools, `mo update` and the installer no longer pop up the Command Line Tools installer, and both fall back to Git release tags when the GitHub API lookup fails.\n8. **Stop commands that ignore Ctrl-C**: A command that ignores the stop signal is now force-stopped two seconds after its time limit, so a stuck step can no longer hang a cleanup or uninstall.\n9. **Cleaner `mo remove`**: It removes Mole's shell completion lines, keeps your own lines and rc symlinks intact, and exits with an error when no terminal can confirm the removal.\n10. **Smoother Analyze and Purge**: Analyze keeps every entry browsable and refreshes a folder that changed right after its scan, and Purge re-scans a slow container folder one project at a time instead of skipping later artifacts.\n\n### 更新日志\n\n1. **在 Apple Silicon 上给通用 App 瘦身**：`mo slim` 会删掉你自己装的 App 里的 Intel 代码，每个 App 都先在副本上处理，副本通过代码签名和 Gatekeeper 检查后才替换原 App，原 App 移到废纸篓，整个过程不需要开发者工具，可以先用 `mo slim --dry-run` 预览。\n2. **让 AI Agent 帮你用 Mole**：官方 Mole skill 会让 Claude Code、Codex、Cursor 等 Agent 每次清理前先用 `--dry-run` 预览，卸载 App 和需要管理员权限的步骤留给你自己来，安装命令是 `npx skills add tw93/Mole -a claude-code codex cursor -g -y`。\n3. **卸载时默认选中个人数据**：`mo uninstall --with-data <名字>` 一开始就选中 App 的设置和数据，预览里仍会逐条列出，按 D 可以保留任意一条路径。\n4. **清理更多 App 残留**：clean 现在能清理飞书及其沙盒缓存、微信的网页 profile、闲置的 Helium 签名副本，以及富途牛牛关闭时留下的更新安装包。\n5. **外置硬盘清理更准确**：`mo clean --external` 报告的是实际清理出的空间，保留硬盘上的废纸篓和受保护的 Finder 元数据，临时目录里有读不到的子目录时也会照常计算大小，不再整项跳过。\n6. **卸载确认更稳妥**：Homebrew cask 的密码提示保持在前台，真实卸载必须在终端里确认，没有终端时的 dry run 列出计划后正常结束，名字里带控制字符的 App 也能安全显示。\n7. **更新时不再弹出命令行工具安装框**：没装开发者工具的 Mac 上，`mo update` 和安装脚本不会再弹出 Command Line Tools 安装框，GitHub API 查不到版本时也会改用 Git 的 release tag。\n8. **忽略 Ctrl-C 的命令也能停下**：某条命令不响应停止信号时，超过时间限制两秒后会被强制结束，清理和卸载不会再卡在这一步。\n9. **`mo remove` 卸得更干净**：会删掉 Mole 写入的 shell 补全行，保留你自己的配置行和 rc 文件的软链，没有终端可以确认时以错误退出。\n10. **Analyze 和 Purge 更顺手**：Analyze 的每一项都能继续浏览，扫描后马上有变化的目录也会刷新，Purge 遇到扫描很慢的容器目录时会逐个项目重扫，不再跳过后面的构建产物。\n\n### Thanks\n\nIssue reporters and PR contributors this cycle: @viniciusdsandrade · @HangLark · @M-Hassan-Raza · @greyby · @r266-tech · @Showdown76py · @ragnarok22 · @Ctrl-Alb.\n\n### Mole Mac App\n\nIf you would rather work in a window than a terminal, [Mole Mac App](https://mole.fit/) covers cleaning, app removal, maintenance, disk analysis and live status, shows everything before it deletes, and adds tools in the menu bar. It costs $19 once, with free updates and a 14-day refund, and you can [download it here](https://mole.fit/download). The CLI stays free and open source.\n",
